    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43385" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐανά-κλητος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>easy to call out</i>, of
			the names of dogs, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				7.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>easy to recall</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς τὸ κοινὸν συμφέρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Cim.</u>
					17
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. ἑαυτὸν παρέχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>TG</u>
					2
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐανακλήτως, διακεῖσθαι πρός τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					M.Ant.
					1.7
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>easily cured</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>SD</u>
				1.7
			</span></i>.</div>
